cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Nemesis Analyst
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Obi
    given-names: Ebuka David
repository-code: "https://github.com/eobi/Nemesis_analyst"
abstract: >-
  AI-assisted malware unpacking and analysis. Runs a packed Windows sample under
  a debugger inside a disposable VM over SSH, captures the unpacked payload,
  recovers encryption keys, classifies the malware family, and exports a
  detection package (YARA, Sigma, Suricata, STIX, IOCs). Driveable from any LLM
  via the Model Context Protocol.
keywords:
  - malware analysis
  - reverse engineering
  - unpacking
  - dynamic analysis
  - x64dbg
  - threat intelligence
  - model context protocol
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
